62,3,1,talk,Servas,,"Option A offers precision, but as May noted, the cost is steep. Option B brings a certain peace of mind, though we must ensure it doesn't lead to waste or hidden burdens.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Option C is the simplest, but I'm worried it might continue the tensions I saw in the payment log. If the bills swing wildly, a flat share might still feel unfair to some.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minato,,"Option C seems very easy, but I'm worried it won't solve the problem of people feeling like they are paying for others. I want a way that makes everyone feel it's truly fair.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,May,,"Option C is just a recipe for more stress! With those wild swings I saw in the statements, a flat share means we're all just guessing every month. It's not a real solution.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I think Option C is the easiest to manage, but May is right about the stress. However, Option A sounds like a nightmare to set up and maintain... and Option B still needs a big settlement at the end.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Daisuke, the settlement at the end is but a small price for a winter of tranquility. If we choose a flat share, those in the colder rooms may suffer in silence to avoid being a burden.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, I agree that we need to protect those in colder rooms. But I'm more worried about the emotional cost. If we go with Option C, we might just keep avoiding the real conversations about money and resentment.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Midori, I agree. If we just divide it equally, will the people who use less feel like they are carrying others? I want us to have a system where everyone feels okay and no one is secretly sad.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, being ""okay"" is great, but being broke is worse! Option A is out because of that electrician's quote—we can't just drop a fortune upfront. Option B actually lets us budget, which is a lifesaver when February hits.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree that Option A is too expensive. But @May, if we do Option B, who has to track the difference all year and do the big calculation at the end? I'm worried that part will be really stressful.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@Daisuke, we can share that burden, or find a simple way to track it together. It is better to spend a few hours once a year than to spend every winter day wondering if we are being a burden to our friends.","{""words"":42,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Daisuke, I think we can find a way to share the work so it doesn't fall on one person. I'm leaning toward Option B because it provides stability and prevents those monthly arguments that I'm so worried about.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I think Option B sounds nice because it's more stable. If we can find a way to share the work so Daisuke isn't worried, it might stop the rumors about people carrying each other. I want us to be friends.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,May,,"@Daisuke, we can just use a simple spreadsheet! It's way better than the stress of a 30,000 yen bill hitting us out of nowhere. Option B is the only one that actually lets us plan our lives.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I guess if we all agree to help with the spreadsheet, it might be okay. I just don't want one person to be stuck doing it all alone. If we can really share the work, Option B seems... okay.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Servas,,"It is heartening to see us reach this understanding. By choosing Option B, we embrace a path of stability and kindness, ensuring no one shivers in silence. I shall gladly vote for Option B.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Midori,,I agree. Option B gives us the stability we need to stop the monthly friction and protects our friendships from the stress of fluctuating bills. I'll vote for Option B.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'm happy that we're all agreeing and being so kind to each other. I think Option B is the best way to make sure everyone feels fair and peaceful. I'll vote for Option B too!,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,May,,I'm totally on board! Option B saves us from the financial rollercoaster and doesn't require a massive payment to an electrician. It's the smartest move for all of us. I vote for Option B!,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I'm still a little nervous about the work, but since everyone is being so supportive, I'll trust you all. I'll vote for Option B too.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
